Reviewed each unit against the semantic-linefeeds rule (one sentence per line; rejoin before splitting when a wrap finding shares the line with a fused one; split long lines only at genuine clause boundaries; never sever a token like `:=`).

Unit 8 is the one exception: none of the offered candidates fully resolve the window into one-sentence-per-line — every candidate leaves at least one output line holding two sentences (e.g. "...decoding. Even if float values are supported," fused together). The correct repair — splitting all four sentence boundaries — isn't on the list.

